Patch 2514 (after 2048): a shadow map compared through an A8R8G8B8 view (J-Stars' two maps) is read as the depth
surface itself (R24_UNORM_X8 SRV, the OffDS sampled directly, tex_ds <= -2), as the v0.15 port did, instead of its
colour copy whose A/R/G bytes the shader put back together (_rsx_d24). The game's sampler for the maps is linear;
a lookup off a texel centre mixed the bytes of two depths into a wrong one. SHADOW_DEPTH_DIRECT=0 restores the
byte copy.

Tested (US disc): see the J-Stars STATUS entry for the feature build with this patch.

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
index 687059a4..881cbb8a 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
@@ -2859,6 +2859,16 @@ static u32 fp_txp_units_at(u32 off)
     }
     return units;
 }
+/* SHADOW_DEPTH_DIRECT (patch 2514, default on; =0 the byte copy of 2048): a shadow map compared through an
+ * A8R8G8B8 view is read as the depth surface itself (R24_UNORM_X8), as the v0.15 port did, instead of the colour
+ * copy whose A/R/G bytes the shader put back together (_rsx_d24). The game's sampler for the map is linear, and any
+ * lookup that was not exactly on a texel centre mixed the bytes of two depths into a wrong one. */
+static int shadow_depth_direct(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char* e = getenv("SHADOW_DEPTH_DIRECT"); on = (e && *e == '0') ? 0 : 1; }
+    return on;
+}
 static int zargb_txp_on(void)
 {
